# Personal / session-local artifacts not part of the repo.
# Everything under .claude is local (settings.local.json, caches) EXCEPT
# skills: those are working-style instructions meant to travel with the repo,
# so the same rules apply on any clone. Written as `.claude/*` rather than
# `.claude/`, because git cannot re-include a path whose parent DIRECTORY is
# excluded — the negation below is silently dead with a trailing slash.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
CLAUDE.local.md
dba-slack-bot-handoff.md
slack_token_rotation_audit.md
metrics_dashboard.html
# design-canvas tool state (not part of the handoff)
QueryHubWeb/.design-canvas.state.json
QueryHubWeb/.thumbnail
# design-tool component-library export (not needed to run the frontend)
QueryHubWeb/_ds/

# Vite frontend: deps AND build output stay out of git. The deploy builds
# dist/ (scripts/install.sh does it; deploy/INSTALL.md documents it), and the
# web app now serves an explicit "frontend not built" page instead of silently
# falling back to a CDN prototype its own CSP blocks.
QueryHubWeb/app/node_modules/
QueryHubWeb/app/.vite/
QueryHubWeb/app/dist/

# local reference copy of the previous prototype drop
QueryHubWeb_old/

# Python build artifacts (setuptools)
build/

# Coverage artifacts (CI measures coverage; the data file is local).
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
